We have an **OpenFin runtime on client machines, which hosts our React application using an embedded Chromium engine.
In the earlier setup, the React app connected directly to Solace using the Solace JavaScript client over secure WebSocket (mTLS), and received real-time data via pub-sub topics.
In the new architecture, Solace has been removed. The React app now connects to a backend Java service using WebSocket (wss).
This backend is a long-running service (built using Guava/Guice) that acts as a gateway—it communicates with downstream systems using gRPC and streams data back to the UI over WebSocket.